tion_ids":["cite.long.prop-one-orbit"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-one-orbit"],"id":"long.prop-one-orbit","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 8.1 (Stability of each fixed greedy prefix)","locator":"Long record Proposition 8.1, p. 93, label prop:one-orbit","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $t_j\\to1/2$ and, for each fixed $n\\ge2$, let $v_n^{(j)}\\to x_n=(2^n-1)^{-1}$, with $v_n^{(j)}>0$. Apply the greedy rule with target $t_j$ and weights $v_n^{(j)}$ in increasing order of $n$, through depths $m_j\\to\\infty$. For every fixed depth $K$, the decisions at ranks $2,\\ldots,K$ eventually agree with those of the real half-greedy rule. This assertion concerns finite prefixes, not survival at all ranks.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-one-orbit","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-one-orbit","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-one-orbit%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.approx_orbit_induction%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-one-orbit%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.approx_orbit_induction%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.approx_orbit_induction"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-one-orbit","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-one-orbit%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_one_o